The main advantage of RAG is that it allows the model to leverage the knowledge and facts from a larger corpus, which can improve the quality and accuracy of its responses, especially for open-domain tasks where there may not be enough training data. However, it also increases the latency since the model has to perform the retrieval step first, making it less suitable for real-time applications with strict time constraints.
