[99/200] Running: How are model prompts structured in ChatML?...

🧠 LLM Response:


In ChatML, model prompts are defined as `prompt` elements within a `model` element. Here's a basic example:

```xml
<models>
    <model id="model1">
        <name>Simple Question Answering Model</name>
        <description>A model for answering simple questions.</description>
        <prompt>What is the capital of France?</prompt>
    </model>
</models>
```

In this example, the `prompt` element contains the question the model will be asked to answer. The `name`, `description` elements are optional and can be used to provide additional information about the model.

You can also use variables in your prompts. For example:

```xml
<prompt>What is the capital of {country}?</prompt>
```

In this case, you would need to provide a variable for the `country` within the context of the conversation, for example:

```json
{
    "context": {
        "country": "France"
    }
}
```

You can also define multiple prompts for a single model, in case the model can handle multiple tasks or types of questions:

```xml
<prompts>
    <prompt>What is the capital of {country}?</prompt>
    <prompt>Describe the concept of {concept}.</prompt>
</prompts>
```
