[101/200] Running: How do you batch requests for high throughput?...

🧠 LLM Response:


One approach for batching requests for high throughput is to use a message broker or queueing system. In this approach, when a client sends a request, instead of sending it directly to the required service, it is first added to a queue. Multiple requests can be added to the same queue. A worker process is responsible for taking requests from the queue and processing them. This allows for parallel execution of requests, as multiple workers can be handling requests from the same queue at the same time.

Another approach is to use a cache layer that caches the responses of frequently accessed requests and serves them directly to the client, bypassing the service entirely. This can help to avoid making the same request multiple times, reducing the overall load on the service.

The choice of approach will depend on factors such as the nature of the requests, the scalability needs of the system, and performance requirements.
