5. **Monitoring and evaluating the model**: After the vLLM is deployed, it's crucial to monitor its performance and ensure it works as intended. You may track the model's latency, accuracy, and other metrics, and implement solutions to address any performance issues or drift over time. Additionally, continue to gather and label new data to retrain the model regularly to maintain its accuracy.

Serving transformers-based models with vLLMs can pave the way for developing powerful NLP applications, enabling users to leverage cutting-edge language models within their own systems.
