To benchmark with different model precisions, you can use the `torch.backends.cudnn.benchmark = False` setting to make the CUDA backend use precise Floating-Point arithmetic (FP32) instead of faster, mixed-precision arithmetic (FP16 or INT8). This will ensure that the benchmarking is done with the same precision as your training and inference code.

